# The RSI runner's build context — the same rules as the root `.dockerignore`.
#
# Two files rather than one because BuildKit reads THIS one and ignores the
# root, while the classic builder does the reverse. Letting them drift means
# the protection depends on which builder happens to run (#308).
#
# scripts/check-build-context.py fails if their rule sets diverge — in content
# or in order, because Docker resolves a path by the last rule that matches it.
# Edit both or neither.

# ---- VCS metadata --------------------------------------------------------
# `.git` carries every secret ever committed and later removed, which is the
# whole point of history. The RSI runner bakes a fresh repo from the copied
# tree instead of inheriting one.
/.git

# ---- Virtual environments and caches ------------------------------------
# Large, host-specific, and `.venv` can hold credentials cached by tooling.
/.venv
**/.venv
/venv/
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
/.pytest_cache
/.mypy_cache
/.ruff_cache
/.hypothesis
**/node_modules
**/.next
**/.turbo

# ---- Build and test output ----------------------------------------------
**/dist
# ...except the one generated bundle a build actually needs. This root file
# also governs `docker build -f packages/hive-conductor/backend/Dockerfile .`,
# and that Dockerfile copies `frontend/dist/`. Without the exception `**/dist`
# strips it from the context and the backend image fails at its COPY, after
# the base image and the apt layer are already built (Codex, #510).
!packages/hive-conductor/frontend/dist
!packages/hive-conductor/frontend/dist/**
**/build
**/*.egg-info
**/.coverage
**/coverage.xml
**/htmlcov
bandit.json
semgrep.json

# ---- Local run data ------------------------------------------------------
# RSI reports hold exported patches, promotion records and scorecards from
# previous runs. Copying them in would hand a candidate the full history of
# every candidate before it.
/rsi-reports/
**/rsi-reports/
/.conductor/
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
population.db

# ---- Editor and OS noise -------------------------------------------------
**/.DS_Store
**/*.swp
/.idea/
/.vscode/

# ---- Secrets. The reason this file exists. LAST ON PURPOSE. --------------
# Docker resolves a path by the LAST rule that matches it, so a re-inclusion
# written below a denial wins. `!packages/hive-conductor/frontend/dist/**` is
# one, and above it sat every secret rule -- so a `.env` under that path would
# have been re-included by an exception written for a JavaScript bundle
# (Codex, #510). Putting the secret denials last makes them final by
# construction: no exception can be added later without being visibly written
# beneath them.
#
# `.env` holds the database password, the LiteLLM gateway key and every
# provider key the deployment has. `.env.example` is deliberately NOT denied:
# it ships as documentation and carries no value.
.env
.env.*
**/.env
**/.env.*
!.env.example
!**/.env.example
gateway.env
**/gateway.env
# Each private-key pattern is written twice. Docker matches relative to the
# context root, so a bare `*.p12` denies `client.p12` and NOT
# `packages/provider/client.p12` -- and this build copies the whole `packages`
# tree, so the recursive form is the one that was doing the work (Codex, #510).
*.pem
**/*.pem
*.p12
**/*.p12
*.pfx
**/*.pfx
id_rsa*
**/id_rsa*
id_ed25519*
**/id_ed25519*
*.age
**/*.age
.age-key*
**/.age-key*
recovery-phrase*
**/recovery-phrase*
/secrets/
**/secrets/
# Top-level only: `**/vault/` would strip
# packages/maistro-core/tests/vault/ out of every image. An operator's vault
# directory lives at the root; a package named for the subsystem it tests does
# not stop being source because of its name.
/vault/
